From: Build compatibility fix
Subject: [PATCH] Include string.h in the legacy compiler probe

GMP 4.2.1's compiler probe calls memcpy without declaring it. GCC 15 treats
that implicit declaration as an error, causing configure to reject a working
cross compiler.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/acinclude.m4
+++ b/acinclude.m4
@@ -518,2 +518,3 @@
    this compiler+flags.  */
+#include <string.h>
 struct try_t
